{
 "description": "DSSE verification vectors (gate 4, backlog #24). The reference engine pins Ed25519 (RFC 8032); payload = the Attestation's canonical form (annotations excluded); signature input = PAE(payloadType, payload) per DSSE v1. Fixture seed = sha256('jascon dsse fixture key 1'); PUBLIC KEY (hex) embedded in trusted-keys. Digests and signatures are LITERALS - re-run the authoring script after any object edit (it fails loudly, never silently). path-vectors (2026-11-15): where an `envelope-ref` may point - a relative path that stays in the manifest's folder (`beside`: true), or one that leaves it (false): a scheme or drive letter, a leading slash, a backslash or a `..` segment. A ref that leaves the folder does not resolve, whether or not the file it names exists. One pattern in the reference (OUTSIDE_REF), the twin, the app (jscPlainPath) and the reader (besideName). bundle-vectors: a bundle on disk - `listed` objects under objects/ in a manifest the harness writes, `attestation` beside the manifest as attestation.json, `envelopes` by relative path in the manifest's folder, `outside` in the folder above it. `expected-fails` are fragments, one per failure, and no other failure; `expected-envelope` is unverified (read, payload good, no trusted key) or missing (not read). Written by drafts/phase-d/envelope_ref_vectors.py.",
